// CoronaProgramsPC.cpp  (pc/gcm/renderengine)
//
// [PC platform leaf] GENERATED FILE -- do not hand-edit. Regenerate with the
// recipe recorded below.
//
// The corona (head/tail-light FLARE sprite) vertex/pixel programs are, like the
// sky dome's pair and the post-fx programs, NOT in SHADERS.BNDL: they are
// executable-embedded guest .rdata blobs handed straight to the Xenos
// program-buffer registrar by renderengine::CoronaRenderer::Initialize
// @0x822850F8 --
//     vertex : unk_8200F2A0, 788 bytes (the asm stores 0x314 at +0x08)
//     pixel  : unk_8200F1B8, 228 bytes (the asm stores 0xE4  at +0x08)
// Being Xenos microcode inside the guest image they have no PC counterpart and
// nothing in the converted asset tree supplies one.
//
// These two arrays are the SAME two programs recompiled for D3D9. Unlike the
// sky dome's pair -- which was matched to existing TUB HLSL -- there is no TUB
// source for the corona programs, so they were AUTHORED from the Xenos decode,
// the same route the post-fx and Godray shaders took:
//     tools/assets/shaders/brn_corona.fx  (entries mainCoronaVS / mainCoronaPS)
// Every ALU line in that .fx carries the instruction number of its counterpart
// in the disassembly (tools/assets/shaders/xenos.py; full annotated listing in
// scratch/coronas_step1/coronaprogs/work/DECODE.md).
//
// The constant surface is the CTAB interned in the console packages themselves
// (tools/assets/shaders/ctab.py) and the generator RE-CHECKS the recompiled
// CTAB against it name-for-name and register-for-register:
//     vertex : c0 viewProjectionMatrix (4 regs, D3DXPC_MATRIX_ROWS)
//              c4 cameraPositionPlusBrightness   c5 viewXyScale
//     pixel  : s0 coronaTexture (sampler2D)
// Those three vertex names are exactly the three
// ProgramBuffer::GetVariableHandleByName strings CoronaRenderer::Initialize
// resolves (asm 0x82285250 / 0x82285268 / 0x82285280).
//
// Build recipe (identical to tools/assets/shaders/convert_shaders_bundle.py ::
// compile_entry, so these blobs match every other converted PC program; /Zpr
// (row-major packing) is load-bearing AND proven for this pair -- the console
// CTAB declares viewProjectionMatrix as D3DXPC_MATRIX_ROWS and the microcode
// combines c0..c3 as rows, so fxc's column-major default would transpose it):
//     fxc /nologo /T vs_3_0 /E mainCoronaVS /O2 /Zpr /Fo corona_vs.fxo brn_corona.fx
//     fxc /nologo /T ps_3_0 /E mainCoronaPS /O2 /Zpr /Fo corona_ps.fxo brn_corona.fx
// then wrapped by tools/assets/shaders/shader_transcode.py ::
// build_pc_program_buffer(bytecode, shader_type) into platform-4
// ShaderProgramBuffer primary images (0x14-byte ProgramBufferData header +
// D3D9 bytecode at +0x14 + 8-byte ProgramVariableDescriptor table rebuilt from
// the bytecode's CTAB + interned NUL name strings). Only the primary is
// carried: muMicrocodePart3 is 0, there is no Xenos physical block.
//
// THE SIZES BELOW ARE THE *PC IMAGE* SIZES, NOT THE X360 MICROCODE SIZES.
// renderengine::ProgramBufferPC_Adopt bounds-checks the image against the size
// it is handed, so the consumer must pass gu*ProgramPCSize (or sizeof() of the
// array), never the console's 788 / 228.
//
// Provenance:
//     fxc.exe   C:\Program Files (x86)\Windows Kits\10\bin\10.0.26100.0\x64
//               (Microsoft (R) Direct3D Shader Compiler 10.1, file version
//               10.0.26100.4654)
//     raw D3D9 bytecode   736 bytes vertex / 212 bytes pixel
//     wrapped primaries   848 bytes vertex / 256 bytes pixel
//     generated           2026-08-17
// =============================================================================

